# Rule Authoring

Create or update a rule when the user asks to remember a convention, or when the same instruction will matter across many tasks. Skip one-off details, temporary experiments, and a change that only applies to a single edit.

- Save `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` with YAML frontmatter.
- `alwaysApply: true` only for short guidance needed every turn. Otherwise `alwaysApply: false`. If it is unclear which one applies, ask.
- File-specific rules need `globs`. If the pattern is unclear, ask for one such as `**/*.tsx` or `src/app/admin/**/*.ts`.
- One concern per rule. Use short bullets. Add one concrete example when it removes ambiguity.

- "以后都按这个方式写 rule" → create or update a rule.
- "React 组件都遵循这套约定" → `globs: **/*.tsx`.
- "这次把按钮改成蓝色" → change the code only.
